#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5793f07d-e0de-5707-a5e1-32d657244e0b" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Intersections of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70258a9c-ad3c-5850-8748-1f4a0d3a1177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/df/df4a1ecffe6302ee57250944ec8f178f46a066b2edff2ed1afb200e7b0217cf7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282651} {:answer/id #uuid "8e44c058-ebf0-58a9-b42c-cf19c1b27b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6b/6b5b39546eabacdf948bd87e793727fdc8cd8f2664df037be53bfb630fc41670.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282922} {:answer/id #uuid "9b97d722-59cf-5bfa-b1e2-78edadab4a20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/17/17a176a0e7cb254483d93741cd2c1e3db581005f479928ac36809e55bc970c07.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283047} {:answer/id #uuid "e63db0fe-0384-58ea-87bc-2b3a3a552ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∅,$ the empty set" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283695} {:answer/id #uuid "f5247f03-9735-58c9-b61d-6fb0019f18b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/50/506d86848903de9f038d541152aabf67d99d0f4d0a7e5f5772b811ff1cf9dade.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e63db0fe-0384-58ea-87bc-2b3a3a552ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∅,$ the empty set" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283695} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9980425-ccef-5f6c-bf0f-d1c5beef9b70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30b7b0c8-79fe-53ad-bb30-601d2f7e078d" :question/math-academy-id "q-172690" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [0,i].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}=\\{1\\}\\times [0,1]=\\{(1,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/71/71dd97607df48caf579c2e476520507ede035f65c336064f022cd900b6c120fc.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [0,i]=\\{(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,i).$ \n\n![](images/4b/4b87c830620f54e5b3a3bb7923be971b4d9d4abb98cfb3dcdc8387f376a0b452.png)\n\nThere are no points that lie in all sets. Therefore, the intersection of the indexed sets is $∅,$ the empty set."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198272 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3a2b291-c6dd-58c8-a10f-d851511d7bfc" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d39a817-0adb-550e-8e47-c0b77a693527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/68/687ed490e4b4bf72689bc2da100a5ec01d4d853fbf9d1a5297cb288e40774d1e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285050} {:answer/id #uuid "2cbee043-5ba2-528d-8aee-063f374c9411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e4298479aa0cdbbdb394b08e921fb42c4de25deab1f08874d0de0144bbad9053.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285182} {:answer/id #uuid "390fc2d2-01dd-5e3c-a297-12c139db3beb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/76/761e56f14b968a8485c5acf6c648fe04448d374d0f2375f0b5e473953262e958.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285322} {:answer/id #uuid "5986320c-c7fe-52ac-83d2-f4c986dd6a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/34770ca1c57cf00c5779a435dbbc72bf74e024433d8210ce0ea912a22f51008a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285606} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab43c53-7822-528e-ada6-d161755d6289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a1/a1a9065f9dbb6648100bc6a22bff367916c241dc2eba5f3878d6cf1b9821d4e8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ab43c53-7822-528e-ada6-d161755d6289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a1/a1a9065f9dbb6648100bc6a22bff367916c241dc2eba5f3878d6cf1b9821d4e8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286059} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cb2ecd2-7336-5c6e-953e-301306a51187" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd0c147c-869f-5ac6-b075-b382d08ceaa2" :question/math-academy-id "q-181960" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=[0,2]\\times {-1,0,1}$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=[0,2]\\times {-1,0,1}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is either $-1,0,$ or $1.$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2],\\,y\\in {-1,0,1}}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $-1$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(x,-1)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de9bd6dc79cabf8230b0cec26233958aa0fbb001875b9942cbb7f4d36e6b08fb.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $0.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}={(x,0)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/81/819c31e4d29dbd3e18c7dea8df495a565d2ede866ec019c764704d6dc47f5c70.png)\n\nNow, consider ${S}_{3}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{3}={(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/3f/3f335df98dc9cb33ccc96f87d24efa3bd78a4d4c271d0fbaf7ae5e8c30916d9e.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the three line segments shown below.\n\n![](images/a1/a1a9065f9dbb6648100bc6a22bff367916c241dc2eba5f3878d6cf1b9821d4e8.png)"}]}
